IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`
IMPORT `dg4-s204-ratification`

-- Tests of dg4-s204-ratification.l4. Expected values are written by hand from the text of s 204
-- (de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt, lines 671-731), beside each assertion, never copied from the module's own output.

§ `Tests of s 204`

§§ `(a): shielded if ratified as the section provides or validated by the Court`

-- src:672: no defective corporate act or putative stock shall be void or voidable solely as a result of a failure of authorization if ratified ... or validated
#ASSERT `s 204(a) the defective corporate act or putative stock is shielded from being void or voidable solely for a failure of authorization` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 204(a) the defective corporate act or putative stock is shielded from being void or voidable solely for a failure of authorization` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 204(a) the defective corporate act or putative stock is shielded from being void or voidable solely for a failure of authorization` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 204(a) the defective corporate act or putative stock is shielded from being void or voidable solely for a failure of authorization` FALSE FALSE)

§§ `(b)(1): the content of the resolutions, (A) to (E)`

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN
      b IS A BOOLEAN
      c IS A BOOLEAN
      d IS A BOOLEAN
      e IS A BOOLEAN
      f IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 204(b)(1) Board resolutions`
`t204 resolutions` a b c d e f MEANS
    `s 204(b)(1) Board resolutions` WITH
        `the defective corporate act or acts to be ratified are stated` IS a
        `the date of each defective corporate act is stated` IS b
        `the acts involved the issuance of shares of putative stock` IS c
        `the number and type of shares of putative stock issued and the date or dates they were purported to have been issued are stated` IS d
        `the nature of the failure of authorization in respect of each act is stated` IS e
        `the approval of the ratification by the board of directors is stated` IS f

-- (A) acts, (B) dates, (C) putative-stock details only if putative stock was issued, (D) nature of failure, (E) approval.
-- arguments: A B involved-putative C D E
#ASSERT `s 204(b)(1) the resolutions state what paragraphs (A) to (E) require` (`t204 resolutions` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 204(b)(1) the resolutions state what paragraphs (A) to (E) require` (`t204 resolutions` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 204(b)(1) the resolutions state what paragraphs (A) to (E) require` (`t204 resolutions` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 204(b)(1) the resolutions state what paragraphs (A) to (E) require` (`t204 resolutions` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 204(b)(1) the resolutions state what paragraphs (A) to (E) require` (`t204 resolutions` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 204(b)(1) the resolutions state what paragraphs (A) to (E) require` (`t204 resolutions` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 204(b)(1) the resolutions state what paragraphs (A) to (E) require` (`t204 resolutions` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE))

§§ `(b)(1): abandonment before the validation effective time`

-- src:679: the resolutions may provide that, at any time before the validation effective time, the board may abandon the ratification
#ASSERT `s 204(b)(1) the resolutions' abandonment provision lets the board abandon the ratification without further action of the stockholders` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 204(b)(1) the resolutions' abandonment provision lets the board abandon the ratification without further action of the stockholders` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 9) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 204(b)(1) the resolutions' abandonment provision lets the board abandon the ratification without further action of the stockholders` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 11) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the same day: the text turns on the time of day, which a day cannot carry (fork F-T)
#ASSERT `s 204(b)(1) the resolutions' abandonment provision lets the board abandon the ratification without further action of the stockholders` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `(b)(1): the board's quorum and vote, with the larger earlier requirement`

-- src:679: the larger requirement of the instruments in effect at the time of the defective act applies, but a director elected by an extinct class or a former stockholder is not required
`t204 requirement, larger earlier one with one excused for each` MEANS
    `s 204(b)(1) Board requirement` WITH
        `directors needed for a quorum under the requirement that applies when the resolutions are adopted` IS 3
        `directors needed to adopt the resolutions under the requirement that applies when the resolutions are adopted` IS 2
        `directors needed for a quorum under the instruments in effect at the time of the defective corporate act` IS 5
        `directors needed to adopt the resolutions under the instruments in effect at the time of the defective corporate act` IS 4
        `of those needed for a quorum, the number elected, appointed or nominated by a class or series with no shares outstanding or by a person no longer a stockholder` IS 1
        `of those needed to adopt, the number elected, appointed or nominated by a class or series with no shares outstanding or by a person no longer a stockholder` IS 0

`t204 requirement, no larger earlier one` MEANS
    `s 204(b)(1) Board requirement` WITH
        `directors needed for a quorum under the requirement that applies when the resolutions are adopted` IS 3
        `directors needed to adopt the resolutions under the requirement that applies when the resolutions are adopted` IS 2
        `directors needed for a quorum under the instruments in effect at the time of the defective corporate act` IS 2
        `directors needed to adopt the resolutions under the instruments in effect at the time of the defective corporate act` IS 1
        `of those needed for a quorum, the number elected, appointed or nominated by a class or series with no shares outstanding or by a person no longer a stockholder` IS 0
        `of those needed to adopt, the number elected, appointed or nominated by a class or series with no shares outstanding or by a person no longer a stockholder` IS 0

-- larger earlier quorum 5 less 1 excused = 4, above the current 3: 4 are needed. Larger earlier vote 4, none excused: 4 needed.
#ASSERT `s 204(b)(1) the number of directors needed for a quorum to adopt the resolutions` `t204 requirement, larger earlier one with one excused for each` EQUALS 4
#ASSERT `s 204(b)(1) the number of directors needed to adopt the resolutions` `t204 requirement, larger earlier one with one excused for each` EQUALS 4
-- the earlier requirement is not larger: the current one (3 and 2) applies
#ASSERT `s 204(b)(1) the number of directors needed for a quorum to adopt the resolutions` `t204 requirement, no larger earlier one` EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `s 204(b)(1) the number of directors needed to adopt the resolutions` `t204 requirement, no larger earlier one` EQUALS 2
-- the boundary: 4 present and 4 in favour just meets 4 and 4
#ASSERT `s 204(b)(1) the board adopted the resolutions with the quorum and vote required` `t204 requirement, larger earlier one with one excused for each` 4 4
#ASSERT NOT (`s 204(b)(1) the board adopted the resolutions with the quorum and vote required` `t204 requirement, larger earlier one with one excused for each` 3 4)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 204(b)(1) the board adopted the resolutions with the quorum and vote required` `t204 requirement, larger earlier one with one excused for each` 4 3)
#ASSERT `s 204(b)(1) the board adopted the resolutions with the quorum and vote required` `t204 requirement, no larger earlier one` 3 2
#ASSERT NOT (`s 204(b)(1) the board adopted the resolutions with the quorum and vote required` `t204 requirement, no larger earlier one` 2 2)

§§ `(b)(2): the initial board of directors`

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN
      b IS A BOOLEAN
      c IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 204(b)(2) Initial board resolutions`
`t204 initial resolutions` a b c MEANS
    `s 204(b)(2) Initial board resolutions` WITH
        `the names of the persons who first took action in the name of the corporation as the initial board of directors are stated` IS a
        `the earlier of the date those persons first took action and the date they were purported to have been elected is stated` IS b
        `the approval of the ratification of their election as the initial board of directors is stated` IS c

-- src:682: (B) the EARLIER of the date they first took action or were purported to have been elected
#ASSERT `s 204(b)(2)(B) the date the resolutions state` (YearMonthDay 2020 5 1) (YearMonthDay 2020 4 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2020 4 1
#ASSERT `s 204(b)(2)(B) the date the resolutions state` (YearMonthDay 2020 4 1) (YearMonthDay 2020 5 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2020 4 1
#ASSERT `s 204(b)(2)(B) the date the resolutions state` (YearMonthDay 2020 4 1) (YearMonthDay 2020 4 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2020 4 1
#ASSERT `s 204(b)(2) the resolutions state what paragraphs (A) to (C) require` (`t204 initial resolutions` TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 204(b)(2) the resolutions state what paragraphs (A) to (C) require` (`t204 initial resolutions` FALSE TRUE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 204(b)(2) the resolutions state what paragraphs (A) to (C) require` (`t204 initial resolutions` TRUE FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 204(b)(2) the resolutions state what paragraphs (A) to (C) require` (`t204 initial resolutions` TRUE TRUE FALSE))
-- a majority of the persons exercising the powers of directors: 3 of 5 is more than half, 2 of 4 is only half
#ASSERT `s 204(b)(2) the persons may ratify the election of the initial board by these resolutions` (`t204 initial resolutions` TRUE TRUE TRUE) 5 3 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 204(b)(2) the persons may ratify the election of the initial board by these resolutions` (`t204 initial resolutions` TRUE TRUE TRUE) 4 2 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 204(b)(2) the persons may ratify the election of the initial board by these resolutions` (`t204 initial resolutions` TRUE TRUE FALSE) 5 5 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- no persons exercising the powers: the counts cannot be a vote, so the text is not covered
#ASSERT `s 204(b)(2) the persons may ratify the election of the initial board by these resolutions` (`t204 initial resolutions` TRUE TRUE TRUE) 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `(c): when the stockholders must approve`

-- src:684-687: submitted to stockholders unless [(1)(A) and (1)(B)] or (2)
-- arguments: route, (1)(A), (1)(B), (2)
#ASSERT `s 204(c) the ratification must be submitted to the stockholders for approval` `ratifying any other defective corporate act under s 204(b)(1)` FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 204(c) the ratification must be submitted to the stockholders for approval` `ratifying any other defective corporate act under s 204(b)(1)` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 204(c) the ratification must be submitted to the stockholders for approval` `ratifying any other defective corporate act under s 204(b)(1)` FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 204(c) the ratification must be submitted to the stockholders for approval` `ratifying any other defective corporate act under s 204(b)(1)` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 204(c) the ratification must be submitted to the stockholders for approval` `ratifying any other defective corporate act under s 204(b)(1)` FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 204(c) the ratification must be submitted to the stockholders for approval` `ratifying any other defective corporate act under s 204(b)(1)` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 204(c) the ratification must be submitted to the stockholders for approval` `ratifying any other defective corporate act under s 204(b)(1)` TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- (c) speaks of acts ratified under (b)(1); the initial board's ratification under (b)(2) is not sent to the stockholders
#ASSERT NOT (`s 204(c) the ratification must be submitted to the stockholders for approval` `ratifying the election of the initial board of directors under s 204(b)(2)` FALSE FALSE FALSE)

§§ `(d)(1): notice of the meeting at least 20 days before it`

GIVEN given IS A DATE
      meeting IS A DATE
      time IS A BOOLEAN
      hasPlace IS A BOOLEAN
      place IS A BOOLEAN
      purpose IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 204(d) Meeting notice`
`t204 notice` given meeting time hasPlace place purpose MEANS
    `s 204(d) Meeting notice` WITH
        `the day notice of the meeting was given` IS given
        `the day of the meeting` IS meeting
        `the notice states the time of the meeting` IS time
        `the meeting has a place` IS hasPlace
        `the notice states the place of the meeting` IS place
        `the notice states the purpose of the meeting` IS purpose
        `the notice contains a copy of the resolutions adopted under paragraph (b)(1)` IS TRUE
        `the notice contains the information required by paragraphs (b)(1)(A) through (E)` IS FALSE
        `the notice contains the statement that a claim must be brought within 120 days from the applicable validation effective time` IS TRUE

-- src:688: given at least 20 days before the date of the meeting. 1 March + 20 days = 21 March, the first day that is enough.
#ASSERT `s 204(d)(1) due notice of the meeting was given at least 20 days before it` (`t204 notice` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 21) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 204(d)(1) due notice of the meeting was given at least 20 days before it` (`t204 notice` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 20) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE))
#ASSERT `s 204(d)(1) due notice of the meeting was given at least 20 days before it` (`t204 notice` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 4 30) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- the notice must state time, purpose and, if there is a place, the place
#ASSERT NOT (`s 204(d)(1) due notice of the meeting was given at least 20 days before it` (`t204 notice` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 21) FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 204(d)(1) due notice of the meeting was given at least 20 days before it` (`t204 notice` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 21) TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 204(d)(1) due notice of the meeting was given at least 20 days before it` (`t204 notice` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 21) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE))
-- "place, if any": a meeting with no place needs no place in the notice
#ASSERT `s 204(d)(1) due notice of the meeting was given at least 20 days before it` (`t204 notice` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 21) TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- across a month end and a leap year: 20 days after 15 February 2028 is 6 March 2028
#ASSERT `s 204(d)(1) due notice of the meeting was given at least 20 days before it` (`t204 notice` (YearMonthDay 2028 2 15) (YearMonthDay 2028 3 6) TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 204(d)(1) due notice of the meeting was given at least 20 days before it` (`t204 notice` (YearMonthDay 2028 2 15) (YearMonthDay 2028 3 5) TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE))

§§ `(d)(3): what the notice contains`

GIVEN copy IS A BOOLEAN
      info IS A BOOLEAN
      statement IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 204(d) Meeting notice`
`t204 notice contents` copy info statement MEANS
    `s 204(d) Meeting notice` WITH
        `the day notice of the meeting was given` IS YearMonthDay 2026 3 1
        `the day of the meeting` IS YearMonthDay 2026 3 21
        `the notice states the time of the meeting` IS TRUE
        `the meeting has a place` IS TRUE
        `the notice states the place of the meeting` IS TRUE
        `the notice states the purpose of the meeting` IS TRUE
        `the notice contains a copy of the resolutions adopted under paragraph (b)(1)` IS copy
        `the notice contains the information required by paragraphs (b)(1)(A) through (E)` IS info
        `the notice contains the statement that a claim must be brought within 120 days from the applicable validation effective time` IS statement

#ASSERT `s 204(d)(3) the notice contains what the paragraph requires` (`t204 notice contents` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 204(d)(3) the notice contains what the paragraph requires` (`t204 notice contents` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 204(d)(3) the notice contains what the paragraph requires` (`t204 notice contents` TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 204(d)(3) the notice contains what the paragraph requires` (`t204 notice contents` FALSE FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 204(d)(3) the notice contains what the paragraph requires` (`t204 notice contents` TRUE TRUE FALSE))

§§ `(d)(1) and (2): who is entitled to the notice`

GIVEN valid IS A BOOLEAN
      putative IS A BOOLEAN
      earlier IS A BOOLEAN
      known IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 204(d) Holder`
`t204 holder` valid putative earlier known MEANS
    `s 204(d) Holder` WITH
        `holds valid stock when notice is given, whether voting or nonvoting` IS valid
        `holds putative stock when notice is given, whether voting or nonvoting` IS putative
        `was a holder of record of valid stock or putative stock as of the time of the defective corporate act or the record date it involved` IS earlier
        `the identity and address can be determined from the records of the corporation` IS known

#ASSERT `s 204(d)(1) and (2) the holder is entitled to notice of the meeting` (`t204 holder` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 204(d)(1) and (2) the holder is entitled to notice of the meeting` (`t204 holder` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 204(d)(1) and (2) the holder is entitled to notice of the meeting` (`t204 holder` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- a holder of record at the time of the act whose identity or address cannot be determined is left out
#ASSERT NOT (`s 204(d)(1) and (2) the holder is entitled to notice of the meeting` (`t204 holder` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 204(d)(1) and (2) the holder is entitled to notice of the meeting` (`t204 holder` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE))

§§ `(d)(4): the vote at the meeting`

-- b.: a majority of the shares present and entitled to vote on the election of the director. 6 of 10 carries; 5 of 10 does not.
#ASSERT `s 204(d)(4)b. the ratification of the election of the director carries by a majority of the votes present` 6 10 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 204(d)(4)b. the ratification of the election of the director carries by a majority of the votes present` 5 10 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 204(d)(4)b. the ratification of the election of the director carries by a majority of the votes present` 11 10 EQUALS NOTHING

GIVEN quorum IS A BOOLEAN
      voteNow IS A BOOLEAN
      director IS A BOOLEAN
      larger IS A BOOLEAN
      largerMet IS A BOOLEAN
      s203 IS A BOOLEAN
      s203Met IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 204(d)(4) Approval facts`
`t204 approval facts` quorum voteNow director larger largerMet s203 s203Met MEANS
    `s 204(d)(4) Approval facts` WITH
        `the quorum required for this type of act when the ratification is approved was present` IS quorum
        `the vote required for this type of act when the ratification is approved was obtained` IS voteNow
        `the defective corporate act is the election of a director` IS director
        `the instruments in effect at the time of the defective corporate act required a larger quorum or vote` IS larger
        `that larger quorum and vote were obtained, leaving out shares of a class or series with no shares outstanding and any person no longer a stockholder` IS largerMet
        `the failure of authorization resulted from a failure to comply with s 203` IS s203
        `the vote set forth in s 203(a)(3) was obtained` IS s203Met

-- arguments: quorum voteNow director larger largerMet s203 s203Met
#ASSERT `s 204(d)(4) the stockholders approved the ratification` (`t204 approval facts` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 204(d)(4) the stockholders approved the ratification` (`t204 approval facts` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 204(d)(4) the stockholders approved the ratification` (`t204 approval facts` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a.: a larger earlier requirement must also be met
#ASSERT `s 204(d)(4) the stockholders approved the ratification` (`t204 approval facts` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 204(d)(4) the stockholders approved the ratification` (`t204 approval facts` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- c.: a failure to comply with s 203 also needs the vote in s 203(a)(3)
#ASSERT `s 204(d)(4) the stockholders approved the ratification` (`t204 approval facts` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 204(d)(4) the stockholders approved the ratification` (`t204 approval facts` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- b.: for a director the majority-of-present test replaces the type's own vote
#ASSERT `s 204(d)(4) the stockholders approved the ratification` (`t204 approval facts` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 204(d)(4) the stockholders approved the ratification` (`t204 approval facts` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 204(d)(4) the stockholders approved the ratification` (`t204 approval facts` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `(d)(5): putative stock neither votes nor counts toward a quorum`

#ASSERT `s 204(d)(5) the shares are entitled to vote and are counted for a quorum in the vote to ratify` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- shares that were not putative stock then: (d)(5) says nothing about them
#ASSERT `s 204(d)(5) the shares are entitled to vote and are counted for a quorum in the vote to ratify` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

